hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15805","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Nawfal ibn Musahiq mentioned it, Sufyan said, and his grandfather was a Badri, from a man from Muzaynah called Ibn Isam, from his father, and he was among the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an expedition he would say: If you see a mosque or hear a caller to prayer, do not kill anyone. Ibn Isam said, from his father: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us in an expedition."
